WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.996
Counter-deception is the defensive practice of reducing the harm caused by misleading claims,

00:00:04.996 --> 00:00:07.633
distorted context, manipulated evidence, and pressure-driven decisions.

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:10.269
In this course, the word defensive matters.

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:14.789
The analyst is not trying to trick an adversary, embarrass a person,

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:16.295
or win an argument.

00:00:16.295 --> 00:00:20.061
The analyst is trying to understand what is being claimed,

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:22.321
what decision depends on that claim,

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:25.711
and what evidence is strong enough to support action.

00:00:25.711 --> 00:00:29.100
Deception works best when people are rushed, emotionally loaded,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.737
or forced to decide with poor context.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:35.503
A suspicious message, a dramatic screenshot, a selective log excerpt,

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:40.776
or a confident intelligence claim can all create momentum before anyone has verified provenance.

00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:44.166
Counter-deception slows that momentum down without freezing the organization.

00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:49.438
The operating question is simple: what do we know, how do we know it,

00:00:49.438 --> 00:00:52.828
what remains uncertain, and what would change the decision?

00:00:52.828 --> 00:00:56.594
This discipline applies across security operations, fraud review, insider risk,

00:00:56.594 --> 00:00:59.231
incident response, threat intelligence, and executive support.

00:00:59.231 --> 00:01:02.997
The same pattern appears in different forms: a claim arrives,

00:01:02.997 --> 00:01:07.140
a source is attached to it, evidence is offered or withheld,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.776
and someone is pushed toward a decision.

00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:14.296
The analyst's job is to separate those pieces, preserve context, test alternatives,

00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:18.062
and communicate confidence in a way decision makers can use.

00:01:18.062 --> 00:01:20.699
Ethical handling is not a side issue.

00:01:20.699 --> 00:01:24.465
A counter-deception review may involve people, accounts, devices, communications, telemetry,

00:01:24.465 --> 00:01:25.595
or sensitive artifacts.

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:30.114
The work should protect privacy, maintain chain of custody, avoid amplifying harm,

00:01:30.114 --> 00:01:31.998
and escalate through approved paths.

00:01:31.998 --> 00:01:34.634
Good counter-deception does not make analysts cynical.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:38.024
It makes them disciplined: curious, careful, transparent about uncertainty,

00:01:38.024 --> 00:01:40.660
and steady enough to verify before reacting.
